      "difficulty_level": "H3",
      "difficulty_reason": "The authors establish coefficient-dimension hardness for every nonzero multiple using leading/trailing diagonals and all-partition embedding, transfer it to read-twice oblivious branching programs, and show a hypothetical roABP-IPS refutation would produce a small read-twice program for a forbidden nonzero multiple. This multiplicative-hardness mechanism is independent of the reciprocal-function method. Its intermediate lower bounds and linear-IPS/subclass consequences are support, not extra counted objects.",
